{
  "id": "m57l1",
  "title": {
    "es": "Hilos con threading",
    "en": "Threads with threading"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Varias tareas a la vez"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`threading.Thread(target=funcion)` crea un hilo; `.start()` lo lanza y `.join()` espera a que termine. Si varios hilos tocan el mismo dato, usa un `Lock` para evitar **condiciones de carrera**."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "import threading",
          "cont = 0",
          "lock = threading.Lock()",
          "def inc():",
          "    global cont",
          "    with lock:",
          "        cont += 1",
          "hilos = [threading.Thread(target=inc) for _ in range(3)]",
          "for h in hilos: h.start()",
          "for h in hilos: h.join()",
          "print(cont)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "3"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "En CPython, los hilos van bien para esperas (E/S); para cálculo puro mira multiprocessing (otro proceso por núcleo)."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Several tasks at once"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`threading.Thread(target=function)` creates a thread; `.start()` launches it and `.join()` waits for it. If several threads touch the same data, use a `Lock` to avoid **race conditions**."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "import threading",
          "cont = 0",
          "lock = threading.Lock()",
          "def inc():",
          "    global cont",
          "    with lock:",
          "        cont += 1",
          "hilos = [threading.Thread(target=inc) for _ in range(3)]",
          "for h in hilos: h.start()",
          "for h in hilos: h.join()",
          "print(cont)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "3"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "In CPython, threads are good for waiting (I/O); for pure computation look at multiprocessing (one process per core)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m57l1e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `contar_con_hilos(n)` que lance n hilos que incrementan un contador con un Lock y devuelva el total.",
        "en": "Define `contar_con_hilos(n)` launching n threads that increment a counter with a Lock and return the total."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "import threading",
        "",
        "def contar_con_hilos(n):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "import threading",
        "",
        "def contar_con_hilos(n):",
        "    cont = 0",
        "    lock = threading.Lock()",
        "    def inc():",
        "        nonlocal cont",
        "        with lock:",
        "            cont += 1",
        "    hilos = [threading.Thread(target=inc) for _ in range(n)]",
        "    for h in hilos:",
        "        h.start()",
        "    for h in hilos:",
        "        h.join()",
        "    return cont"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Crea los hilos, start() a todos, join() a todos; protege el contador con el lock."
        ],
        "en": [
          "Create the threads, start() all, join() all; protect the counter with the lock."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "contar_con_hilos",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                25
              ],
              "expected": 25
            },
            {
              "args": [
                0
              ],
              "expected": 0
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m57l1e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `paralelo(valores)` que calcule el cuadrado de cada valor en su propio hilo y devuelva la lista en orden.",
        "en": "Define `paralelo(valores)` computing each value's square in its own thread and returning the list in order."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "import threading",
        "",
        "def paralelo(valores):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "import threading",
        "",
        "def paralelo(valores):",
        "    res = [None] * len(valores)",
        "    def trabajo(i, v):",
        "        res[i] = v * v",
        "    hilos = [threading.Thread(target=trabajo, args=(i, v)) for i, v in enumerate(valores)]",
        "    for h in hilos:",
        "        h.start()",
        "    for h in hilos:",
        "        h.join()",
        "    return res"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Cada hilo escribe en su propio índice de la lista de resultados."
        ],
        "en": [
          "Each thread writes to its own index in the results list."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "paralelo",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  1,
                  2,
                  3
                ]
              ],
              "expected": [
                1,
                4,
                9
              ]
            },
            {
              "args": [
                []
              ],
              "expected": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}